== S1: a(t) ∝ ‖w_N‖ = √(N·H0), so H·t = 1/2 at all times ==
T1: H0 t0 = 0.500 against 0.950 ± 0.008 (-56 sigma)
T2: DESI DR2 BAO chi2 = 5436 for 12 dof (flat LCDM 10.3 for 11), p = 0e+00

== S2: the drawn slice as our space ==
axis scale factors ∝ √N: mean H·t over the three axes = 0.501
  long   axis: size/long = 1.000–1.000; own rate H_i·t from -0.02 to +1.18
  middle axis: size/long = 0.908–0.959; own rate H_i·t from -0.04 to +1.26
  short  axis: size/long = 0.574–0.620; own rate H_i·t from -0.50 to +1.57
  long axis turns at 14.14 rad per unit log N (γ1 = 14.13): once per ×1.249 in N, i.e. 28.3 radians per e-fold of the scale factor
  shear σ/H (rms spread of the axes' rates over their mean): median 0.77, max 3.64
  measured: σ/H < 4.7e-11 (vector mode), < 1.0e-6 (tensor mode)  =>  off by ≥ 8e+05

